R["en"] += [('(Large, Medium, Airfields, each with ON / OFF;', '(the map always opens empty, with no airport selected, so you are completely free; it shows the night area live: a dark blue veil, dawn and dusk shaded, an orange sunrise / sunset line, and the UTC time at the bottom left. The flight <b>Time</b> — Any, Morning, Day, Dusk or Night — is chosen in the FMS, under Flight type: the app shows in UTC the time to set in MSFS, 30 min before takeoff to get ready (1 h for a wide-body or a flight over 4 h), then takeoff and arrival with the light at arrival; when you pick both departure and arrival, the time is computed so the moment fits both airports (e.g. Dusk: takeoff in daylight, landing just after sunset); the time is sent to SimBrief. In Departure → Arrival, the app also shows whether it is day or night right now at your two airports. In Random / duration, you depart now from the airport you chose (it never changes): the app only offers destinations where it will be the right time on landing (e.g. Night: you land at night). The destinations offered match the chosen aircraft: real airports with a suitable runway for an airliner, large airports for a wide-body) (Large, Medium, Airfields, each with ON / OFF;', "The flight <b>Time</b> —")]

